# VITAL local environment. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# A single `.env` is read by three different consumers locally:
#
# 1. Docker Compose interpolation (docker-compose.yml) — POSTGRES_* below configure the
#    local Postgres container.
# 2. The migration runner (`npm run migrate`, via node --env-file-if-exists=.env) — reads
#    DATABASE_URL.
# 3. Expo / Metro (`expo start`) — reads EXPO_PUBLIC_* and inlines them into the client.
#
# Keep credentials alphanumeric: Compose interpolation and Node's --env-file parser handle
# quoting/escaping differently, so special characters in the password can make the Compose
# value and the DATABASE_URL disagree.

# --- Local Postgres (Docker Compose) ---
POSTGRES_USER=vital
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=vital
POSTGRES_DB=vital
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# --- Migrations / app database connection ---
# Must match the POSTGRES_* values above. In production this is supplied by Doppler as a
# RUN_TIME secret pointing at DO Managed Postgres — never committed here.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://vital:vital@localhost:5432/vital

# --- Expo client ---
# Origin the client calls for API routes. Empty/relative for local web+dev; the deployed
# DO origin for native builds. See app.config.ts and docs/deploy-digitalocean.md.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
